    "created_at": "2016-06-08T17:34:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-09-07T20:27:20Z",
    "body": "I was using the snippet below. Chrome shows an \"In stop: true\" in the console, while Firefox doesn't.\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<script>\r\nvar requests = [];\r\nvar inStop = false;\r\nfunction startRequest() {\r\n  var x = new XMLHttpRequest();\r\n  x.open(\"GET\", location, true);\r\n  x.onabort = startRequest;\r\n  x.send(null);\r\n  requests.push(x);\r\n  console.log(\"In stop: \" + inStop);\r\n}\r\n\r\nstartRequest();\r\ninStop = true;\r\nwindow.stop();\r\ninStop = false;\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
